From 4b31a99af920b32a1b15f3082c5f589be10789b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:11:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] N8 v2 (Round-11 audit correction): per-residue altloc
 selection is the DEFAULT

Audit finding (Round-11, failure 3): the N8 directive required a
per-residue DEFAULT; v1 shipped per_residue as opt-in with per_atom as
the engine default. v2 flips the module default
(ALTLOC_POLICY = ALTLOC_POLICY_PER_RESIDUE) exactly as directed.

- per_residue (DEFAULT): one altloc ID per residue by TOTAL occupancy,
  first-seen ID on ties; blank-altloc shared atoms always kept.
- per_atom (explicit opt-in): the original P0 item 6 rule, kept for
  byte-level comparison with pre-N8 deliveries (altloc_policy=
  ALTLOC_POLICY_PER_ATOM).
- The flip is an audit-directed semantic change, recorded in the
  delivery register; no threshold, law ID, or law meaning is altered.
- Selection logic is unchanged from v1; only the default and the
  tests/documentation change. 3ERD ASP A 321 (0.50/0.50 tie) still
  resolves to conformer A: per-residue totals tie -> first-seen ID.

Tests: tests/test_altloc_selection.py (8) + tests/test_altloc_per_residue.py
(14) = 22; 19 passed / 3 failed in the delivery sandbox, all 3 failures
being the mmCIF tests with ModuleNotFoundError: gemmi (PyPI unreachable
in this sandbox; the identical 2 CIF tests also error under v1 here).
The CIF path shares the same _select_conformers selector as PDB; the
prior-session v1 run reported all 20 tests passing with gemmi present.
Base: science/p0-correctness-2026-10-19 @ ebc1fd79.
